-- Both typecheck-stage warnings in ONE file, so `check --json` pins that they
-- carry DISTINCT `W-*` codes bound to their OWN ranges.
--
-- Why this fixture exists: `diagOfTypeWarning` used to DISCARD the code the
-- TcDiag carried and recompute one by prefix-matching the rendered message, with
-- `otherwise = "W-NONEXHAUSTIVE"`.  Nothing pinned `W-UNREACHABLE-ARM` in
-- `check --json` at all, and nothing pinned the two codes coexisting.
--
-- ⚠️ Honest scope: this fixture CANNOT detect a re-derivation regression, and it
-- does NOT exercise `diagKind` — both shipped codes are exactly what a
-- message-prefix matcher produces, and `codeKind "W-…"` already returns
-- "warning", so every assertion below holds identically with either one reverted.
-- Only a third, non-`W-` code discriminates, and that needs a third warning,
-- which does not exist yet.  What this DOES pin is the coverage gap that made the
-- original defect invisible: that the second code exists in `--json`, that the
-- two codes do not collapse to one, that each binds to its own arm, and that
-- both render `"kind":"warning"` with `"severity":2`.
--
-- Expected values DERIVED BY HAND, not captured-then-accepted:
--   `nonExhaustive` — scrutinee `Color` has ctors Red|Green|Blue; the arms cover
--     Red and Green, so `Blue` escapes every arm => non-exhaustive match.
--     code `W-NONEXHAUSTIVE`, severity 2, kind "warning" (W- => warning), and a
--     `help` naming the missing ctor.
--   `unreachableArm` — the `_` arm is unguarded and range-free, so it covers
--     every value Red did not; the later `Green` arm is therefore provably dead.
--     code `W-UNREACHABLE-ARM`, severity 2, kind "warning", NO help (the hint has
--     no single mechanical edit, so `diagOfTypeWarning` emits no `fix`/`help`).
--   Neither is an error, so `check --json` must still exit 0.
--   Each warning is anchored at its own arm BODY span, so the two ranges differ.

data Color = Red | Green | Blue

nonExhaustive : Color -> Int
nonExhaustive c = match c
  Red => 1
  Green => 2

unreachableArm : Color -> Int
unreachableArm c = match c
  Red => 10
  _ => 20
  Green => 30

main = println (nonExhaustive Red + unreachableArm Blue)
